  "question": {
    "text": "The pressure of an ideal gas varies with volume as $P=\\alpha V$, where $\\alpha$ is a constant. One mole of the gas is allowed to undergo expansion such that its volume becomes ' $m$ ' times its initial volume. The work done by the gas in the process is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cDXyf",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\alpha V}{2}\\left(m^2-1\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "XbJ1S",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\alpha^2 V^2}{2}\\left(m^2-1\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ViE4W",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\left(m^2-1\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "zxm7X",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\alpha V^2}{2}\\left(m^2-1\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $P=\\alpha V$\nWork done, $w=\\int_V^{m V} P d V$\n$=\\int_V^{m V} \\alpha V d V=\\frac{\\alpha V^2}{2}\\left(m^2-1\\right)$.",
    "image": null
  },
